    "text_full": "Skip to Content\n\nPagePlay\n\nGuides\nWhat is a CMS?\nLogging in\nLogging out\nWorking with pages\nWorking with paragraphs\nWorking with photos\nAdd downloadable files\nWorking with your Photobanner\nSite statistics (via Google Analytics)\nYour PagePlay email\nAdding new email accounts\nEmail account limit\nSetting up your email account\nArchiving your old emails\nReset an email account password\nSet an out of office message\nBuy a new domain\nShould you drop the www?\nAdding more users who can edit content\nSupported browsers\nUpdate your mail servers\nSearch engines\nSearch Engine Optimisation tips\nGoogle Search console Verification\nFacebook Like Box / Button\nOpening links in new tabs/windows\nReferrer terms and conditions\nHow do I log in to my site?\n1. Open your web browser and type your website address into the address bar, followed by '/login'\n\nJust add /login to the end of any page of your site to view the login form.\n\nFor example if your website address is:\nhttp://example.com\n\nthen go to\nhttp://example.com/login\n\n2. Enter your email and password\n\nInitially, these will be the email address you used when you signed up along with the password you were assigned.\n\nYou may change these details when you are logged in. Remember, if you change your email address and or password this change will apply to all PagePlay sites you have access to.\n\nForgotten your password?\n\nThat's not a problem, simply click on the \"need a reminder?\" link and enter your email address. You'll then be sent an email with instructions on how to reset your password.\n\nhelp@pageplay.com\n\n© PagePlay Limited, 2026 - Simple Content Management by PagePlay\n\nCookie policy"
